 "date": "2026-10-07",
 "method": "per case, one coronal and one axial slice through the maxillary sinuses (tools/ssb-pipeline/nasalseg/stats.py --png-dir); the uncertain ones again at higher zoom, three coronal levels and an axial slice, window L 0 / W 1400. clear = air fills the bony sinus; thickening = mucosal thickening, cyst, polyp or fluid with air in most of the sinus; opacified = most of the sinus without air; unsure = undecidable, or a label defect. A small sinus with clean walls is clear (hypoplasia is anatomy). Two slices per sinus can miss focal disease elsewhere, so the clear subset can still contain some."
